== Match report ==

=== Balboa 3–0 Nusaraya ===
[[Balboa national football team|Balboa]] comfortably advanced past [[Nusaraya national football team|Nusaraya]] in [[Macaio]], with [[Xavi Bonet]] opening the scoring in the 10th minute. [[Kwame Lòrda]] doubled the lead before half-time in the 44th minute, and [[Rafa Torralba]] sealed the win in the 87th minute. Nusaraya struggled to create chances throughout as Balboa controlled possession.

=== Balisca 2–0 Kalisongo ===
[[Balisca national football team|Balisca]] avoided an upset against [[Kalisongo national football team|Kalisongo]] in [[Axarquía]], scoring in the 25th and 77th minutes to seal a 2–0 win. The co-hosts dominated possession but had to be patient against a resilient Kalisongo side before finding the breakthrough.

=== Asikyira 6–1 Louyan ===
[[Asikyira national football team|Asikyira]] produced the most dominant performance of the tournament so far, demolishing [[Louyan national football team|Louyan]] in [[Sanropura]]. Four goals in the opening 16 minutes — from [[Amadou Baal]] (7'), [[Boubacar Sarr]] (8'), [[Idrissa Koné]] (10'), and [[Ousmane Gueye]] (16') — effectively ended the contest before it had begun. [[Kofi Mensah]] added a fifth before half-time (41'), and [[Salif Diarra]] rounded off the scoring in the 89th minute. Louyan managed a consolation goal in the 38th minute.

=== Pangkajene 4–0 Potocsí ===
[[Pangkajene national football team|Pangkajene]] cruised past [[Potocsí national football team|Potocsí]] in [[Castramara]], with [[Andi Akbar]] (12') and [[Muhammad Asri]] (16') giving them an early 2–0 lead. [[Daeng Naba]] added a third six minutes after the break (51'), and [[Andi Fadli]] completed the rout in the 65th minute.

== Summary ==

The second day of the knockout stage produced 16 goals across 4 matches. [[Balboa national football team|Balboa]], [[Balisca national football team|Balisca]], [[Asikyira national football team|Asikyira]], and [[Pangkajene national football team|Pangkajene]] all advanced to the round of 16. Asikyira's 6–1 demolition of Louyan was the standout performance, while Pangkajene's 4–0 win over Potocsí was equally emphatic.

